{"t":"2026-05-28T02:51:52.451Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VUp8iLDsjVGsUvNAr1Dzap","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     2→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     3→\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→Redis pub/sub event taxonomy and CRM event types.\n     6→\n     7→Channel taxonomy from HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md:\n     8→  - agent.status.discovery    — Discovery Engine events (crawl, scoring, digest)\n     9→  - agent.status.application  — Application Engine events (pipeline status)\n    10→  - agent.status.subagent     — Sub-agent execution events (tool_use loop)\n    11→\n    12→Event payload rules:\n    13→  - Every payload is JSON with an `event` field (SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE)\n    14→  - Payloads include pipeline_id, candidate_id, timestamps\n    15→  - No PII in event payloads — use IDs for reference\n    16→\n    17→CRM event types from crm.py docstring + HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md:\n    18→  - APPLICATION_STARTED\n    19→  - JD_PARSED\n    20→  - RESUME_TAILORED\n    21→  - COMPANY_RESEARCHED\n    22→  - CONTACT_FOUND\n    23→  - EMAIL_DRAFTED\n    24→  - APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\n    25→  - SUBMITTED\n    26→  - EMAIL_SENT\n    27→  - EMAIL_OPENED\n    28→  - RESPONDED\n    29→  - INTERVIEW_SCHEDULED\n    30→  - OFFER_RECEIVED\n    31→  - REJECTED\n    32→  - PLACED\n    33→  - PIPELINE_FAILED\n    34→\"\"\"\n    35→\n    36→from __future__ import annotations\n    37→\n    38→import json\n    39→from datetime import datetime, timezone\n    40→from enum import Enum\n    41→from typing import Any, Optional\n    42→from uuid import UUID\n    43→\n    44→import redis.asyncio as aioredis\n    45→from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n    46→\n    47→import structlog\n    48→\n    49→logger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\n    50→\n    51→\n    52→# ─── Pub/Sub Channels ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    53→\n    54→\n    55→class PubSubChannel(str, Enum):\n    56→    \"\"\"\n    57→    Canonical Redis pub/sub channels.\n    58→\n    59→    These are the ONLY allowed channels for agent status events.\n    60→    Any new channel must be added here and documented in HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md.\n    61→    \"\"\"\n    62→\n    63→    # Discovery Engine events\n    64→    DISCOVERY = \"agent.status.discovery\"\n    65→\n    66→    # Application Engine events (pipeline level)\n    67→    APPLICATION = \"agent.status.application\"\n    68→\n    69→    # Sub-agent execution events (Claude tool_use loop)\n    70→    SUBAGENT = \"agent.status.subagent\"\n    71→\n    72→\n    73→# ─── CRM Event Types ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    74→\n    75→\n    76→class CRMEventType(str, Enum):\n    77→    \"\"\"\n    78→    Canonical CRM event types for the application pipeline.\n    79→\n    80→    These events form the auditable timeline for each application.\n    81→    New event types must be added here — no ad-hoc strings in code.\n    82→    \"\"\"\n    83→\n    84→    # Pipeline lifecycle\n    85→    APPLICATION_STARTED = \"APPLICATION_STARTED\"\n    86→    PIPELINE_FAILED = \"PIPELINE_FAILED\"\n    87→\n    88→    # Processing stages\n    89→    JD_PARSED = \"JD_PARSED\"\n    90→    RESUME_TAILORED = \"RESUME_TAILORED\"\n    91→    COMPANY_RESEARCHED = \"COMPANY_RESEARCHED\"\n    92→    CONTACT_FOUND = \"CONTACT_FOUND\"\n    93→    EMAIL_DRAFTED = \"EMAIL_DRAFTED\"\n    94→\n    95→    # Review + submission\n    96→    APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION = \"APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\"\n    97→    REJECTED = \"REJECTED\"\n    98→    SUBMITTED = \"SUBMITTED\"\n    99→    EMAIL_SENT = \"EMAIL_SENT\"\n   100→\n   101→    # Tracking (post-submission)\n   102→    EMAIL_OPENED = \"EMAIL_OPENED\"\n   103→    RESPONDED = \"RESPONDED\"\n   104→    INTERVIEW_SCHEDULED = \"INTERVIEW_SCHEDULED\"\n   105→    OFFER_RECEIVED = \"OFFER_RECEIVED\"\n   106→    PLACED = \"PLACED\"\n   107→\n   108→\n   109→# ─── Event Payload Schemas ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   110→\n   111→\n   112→class BaseEvent(BaseModel):\n   113→    \"\"\"Base schema for all pub/sub events.\"\"\"\n   114→\n   115→    event: str = Field(..., description=\"Event type in SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\")\n   116→    timestamp: str = Field(\n   117→        default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n   118→        description=\"ISO 8601 timestamp\",\n   119→    )\n   120→\n   121→    class Config:\n   122→        extra = \"allow\"\n   123→\n   124→\n   125→class AgentStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n   126→    \"\"\"\n   127→    Application pipeline status event.\n   128→\n   129→    Published to: agent.status.application\n   130→    \"\"\"\n   131→\n   132→    event: str = \"APPLICATION_STATUS\"\n   133→    pipeline_id: str\n   134→    candidate_id: str\n   135→    status: str\n   136→\n   137→\n   138→class PipelineStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n   139→    \"\"\"\n   140→    Pipeline-level status event (used by PipelineDispatcher).\n   141→\n   142→    Published to: agent.status.application\n   143→    \"\"\"\n   144→\n   145→    event: str = \"PIPELINE_STATUS\"\n   146→    pipeline_id: str\n   147→    status: str\n   148→    details: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n   149→\n   150→\n   151→class SubAgentStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n   152→    \"\"\"\n   153→    Sub-agent execution status event.\n   154→\n   155→    Published to: agent.status.subagent\n   156→    \"\"\"\n   157→\n   158→    event: str = \"SUBAGENT_STATUS\"\n   159→    execution_id: str\n   160→    agent_name: str\n   161→    pipeline_id: str\n   162→    status: str\n   163→    attempt: int = 1\n   164→    duration_ms: Optional[int] = None\n   165→\n   166→\n   167→class DigestReadyEvent(BaseEvent):\n   168→    \"\"\"\n   169→    Discovery digest completion event.\n   170→\n   171→    Published to: agent.status.discovery\n   172→    \"\"\"\n   173→\n   174→    event: str = \"DIGEST_READY\"\n   175→    digest_id: str\n   176→    candidate_id: str\n   177→    run_date: str\n   178→    total_discovered: int\n   179→    total_scored: int\n   180→    top_picks_count: int\n   181→    hot_picks_count: int\n   182→\n   183→\n   184→class CrawlStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n   185→    \"\"\"\n   186→    Crawl run status event.\n   187→\n   188→    Published to: agent.status.discovery\n   189→    \"\"\"\n   190→\n   191→    event: str = \"CRAWL_STATUS\"\n   192→    crawl_run_id: str\n   193→    candidate_id: str\n   194→    status: str  # QUEUED, RUNNING, COMPLETED, FAILED\n   195→    jobs_discovered: Optional[int] = None\n   196→    jobs_scored: Optional[int] = None\n   197→    error: Optional[str] = None\n   198→\n   199→\n   200→# ─── Event Publisher ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   201→\n   202→\n   203→async def publish_event(\n   204→    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n   205→    channel: PubSubChannel | str,\n   206→    event: BaseEvent | dict[str, Any],\n   207→) -> int:\n   208→    \"\"\"\n   209→    Publish an event to a Redis pub/sub channel.\n   210→\n   211→    Args:\n   212→        redis_client: Async Redis client\n   213→        channel: Target pub/sub channel (use PubSubChannel enum)\n   214→        event: Event payload (Pydantic model or dict)\n   215→\n   216→    Returns:\n   217→        Number of subscribers that received the message\n   218→    \"\"\"\n   219→    # Normalize channel to string\n   220→    channel_str = channel.value if isinstance(channel, PubSubChannel) else channel\n   221→\n   222→    # Serialize event\n   223→    if isinstance(event, BaseModel):\n   224→        payload = event.model_dump_json()\n   225→    else:\n   226→        payload = json.dumps(event, default=str)\n   227→\n   228→    # Publish\n   229→    subscriber_count = await redis_client.publish(channel_str, payload)\n   230→\n   231→    logger.debug(\n   232→        \"pubsub.event_published\",\n   233→        channel=channel_str,\n   234→        event_type=event.event if isinstance(event, BaseEvent) else event.get(\"event\"),\n   235→        subscribers=subscriber_count,\n   236→    )\n   237→\n   238→    return subscriber_count\n   239→\n   240→\n   241→# ─── Convenience Publishers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   242→\n   243→\n   244→async def publish_application_status(\n   245→    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n   246→    pipeline_id: UUID,\n   247→    candidate_id: UUID,\n   248→    status: str,\n   249→) -> int:\n   250→    \"\"\"Publish an application pipeline status update.\"\"\"\n   251→    event = AgentStatusEvent(\n   252→        pipeline_id=str(pipeline_id),\n   253→        candidate_id=str(candidate_id),\n   254→        status=status,\n   255→    )\n   256→    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.APPLICATION, event)\n   257→\n   258→\n   259→async def publish_subagent_status(\n   260→    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n   261→    execution_id: UUID,\n   262→    agent_name: str,\n   263→    pipeline_id: UUID,\n   264→    status: str,\n   265→    attempt: int = 1,\n   266→    duration_ms: Optional[int] = None,\n   267→) -> int:\n   268→    \"\"\"Publish a sub-agent execution status update.\"\"\"\n   269→    event = SubAgentStatusEvent(\n   270→        execution_id=str(execution_id),\n   271→        agent_name=agent_name,\n   272→        pipeline_id=str(pipeline_id),\n   273→        status=status,\n   274→        attempt=attempt,\n   275→        duration_ms=duration_ms,\n   276→    )\n   277→    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.SUBAGENT, event)\n   278→\n   279→\n   280→async def publish_digest_ready(\n   281→    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n   282→    digest_id: UUID,\n   283→    candidate_id: UUID,\n   284→    run_date: str,\n   285→    total_discovered: int,\n   286→    total_scored: int,\n   287→    top_picks_count: int,\n   288→    hot_picks_count: int,\n   289→) -> int:\n   290→    \"\"\"Publish a digest completion event.\"\"\"\n   291→    event = DigestReadyEvent(\n   292→        digest_id=str(digest_id),\n   293→        candidate_id=str(candidate_id),\n   294→        run_date=run_date,\n   295→        total_discovered=total_discovered,\n   296→        total_scored=total_scored,\n   297→        top_picks_count=top_picks_count,\n   298→        hot_picks_count=hot_picks_count,\n   299→    )\n   300→    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.DISCOVERY, event)\n   301→\n   302→\n   303→async def publish_crawl_status(\n   304→    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n   305→    crawl_run_id: UUID,\n   306→    candidate_id: UUID,\n   307→    status: str,\n   308→    jobs_discovered: Optional[int] = None,\n   309→    jobs_scored: Optional[int] = None,\n   310→    error: Optional[str] = None,\n   311→) -> int:\n   312→    \"\"\"Publish a crawl run status update.\"\"\"\n   313→    event = CrawlStatusEvent(\n   314→        crawl_run_id=str(crawl_run_id),\n   315→        candidate_id=str(candidate_id),\n   316→        status=status,\n   317→        jobs_discovered=jobs_discovered,\n   318→        jobs_scored=jobs_scored,\n   319→        error=error,\n   320→    )\n   321→    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.DISCOVERY, event)\n   322→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4abf431d-40e8-4b65-91bf-402517737050","uuid":"ec3431c4-a926-4ff4-b274-1f587cd32b78","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/backend/observability/events.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n\"\"\"\nRedis pub/sub event taxonomy and CRM event types.\n\nChannel taxonomy from HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md:\n  - agent.status.discovery    — Discovery Engine events (crawl, scoring, digest)\n  - agent.status.application  — Application Engine events (pipeline status)\n  - agent.status.subagent     — Sub-agent execution events (tool_use loop)\n\nEvent payload rules:\n  - Every payload is JSON with an `event` field (SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE)\n  - Payloads include pipeline_id, candidate_id, timestamps\n  - No PII in event payloads — use IDs for reference\n\nCRM event types from crm.py docstring + HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md:\n  - APPLICATION_STARTED\n  - JD_PARSED\n  - RESUME_TAILORED\n  - COMPANY_RESEARCHED\n  - CONTACT_FOUND\n  - EMAIL_DRAFTED\n  - APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\n  - SUBMITTED\n  - EMAIL_SENT\n  - EMAIL_OPENED\n  - RESPONDED\n  - INTERVIEW_SCHEDULED\n  - OFFER_RECEIVED\n  - REJECTED\n  - PLACED\n  - PIPELINE_FAILED\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\nfrom uuid import UUID\n\nimport redis.asyncio as aioredis\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nimport structlog\n\nlogger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\n\n\n# ─── Pub/Sub Channels ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass PubSubChannel(str, Enum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Canonical Redis pub/sub channels.\n\n    These are the ONLY allowed channels for agent status events.\n    Any new channel must be added here and documented in HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Discovery Engine events\n    DISCOVERY = \"agent.status.discovery\"\n\n    # Application Engine events (pipeline level)\n    APPLICATION = \"agent.status.application\"\n\n    # Sub-agent execution events (Claude tool_use loop)\n    SUBAGENT = \"agent.status.subagent\"\n\n\n# ─── CRM Event Types ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass CRMEventType(str, Enum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Canonical CRM event types for the application pipeline.\n\n    These events form the auditable timeline for each application.\n    New event types must be added here — no ad-hoc strings in code.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Pipeline lifecycle\n    APPLICATION_STARTED = \"APPLICATION_STARTED\"\n    PIPELINE_FAILED = \"PIPELINE_FAILED\"\n\n    # Processing stages\n    JD_PARSED = \"JD_PARSED\"\n    RESUME_TAILORED = \"RESUME_TAILORED\"\n    COMPANY_RESEARCHED = \"COMPANY_RESEARCHED\"\n    CONTACT_FOUND = \"CONTACT_FOUND\"\n    EMAIL_DRAFTED = \"EMAIL_DRAFTED\"\n\n    # Review + submission\n    APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION = \"APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\"\n    REJECTED = \"REJECTED\"\n    SUBMITTED = \"SUBMITTED\"\n    EMAIL_SENT = \"EMAIL_SENT\"\n\n    # Tracking (post-submission)\n    EMAIL_OPENED = \"EMAIL_OPENED\"\n    RESPONDED = \"RESPONDED\"\n    INTERVIEW_SCHEDULED = \"INTERVIEW_SCHEDULED\"\n    OFFER_RECEIVED = \"OFFER_RECEIVED\"\n    PLACED = \"PLACED\"\n\n\n# ─── Event Payload Schemas ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass BaseEvent(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Base schema for all pub/sub events.\"\"\"\n\n    event: str = Field(..., description=\"Event type in SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\")\n    timestamp: str = Field(\n        default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        description=\"ISO 8601 timestamp\",\n    )\n\n    class Config:\n        extra = \"allow\"\n\n\nclass AgentStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n    \"\"\"\n    Application pipeline status event.\n\n    Published to: agent.status.application\n    \"\"\"\n\n    event: str = \"APPLICATION_STATUS\"\n    pipeline_id: str\n    candidate_id: str\n    status: str\n\n\nclass PipelineStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n    \"\"\"\n    Pipeline-level status event (used by PipelineDispatcher).\n\n    Published to: agent.status.application\n    \"\"\"\n\n    event: str = \"PIPELINE_STATUS\"\n    pipeline_id: str\n    status: str\n    details: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n\n\nclass SubAgentStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sub-agent execution status event.\n\n    Published to: agent.status.subagent\n    \"\"\"\n\n    event: str = \"SUBAGENT_STATUS\"\n    execution_id: str\n    agent_name: str\n    pipeline_id: str\n    status: str\n    attempt: int = 1\n    duration_ms: Optional[int] = None\n\n\nclass DigestReadyEvent(BaseEvent):\n    \"\"\"\n    Discovery digest completion event.\n\n    Published to: agent.status.discovery\n    \"\"\"\n\n    event: str = \"DIGEST_READY\"\n    digest_id: str\n    candidate_id: str\n    run_date: str\n    total_discovered: int\n    total_scored: int\n    top_picks_count: int\n    hot_picks_count: int\n\n\nclass CrawlStatusEvent(BaseEvent):\n    \"\"\"\n    Crawl run status event.\n\n    Published to: agent.status.discovery\n    \"\"\"\n\n    event: str = \"CRAWL_STATUS\"\n    crawl_run_id: str\n    candidate_id: str\n    status: str  # QUEUED, RUNNING, COMPLETED, FAILED\n    jobs_discovered: Optional[int] = None\n    jobs_scored: Optional[int] = None\n    error: Optional[str] = None\n\n\n# ─── Event Publisher ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nasync def publish_event(\n    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n    channel: PubSubChannel | str,\n    event: BaseEvent | dict[str, Any],\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Publish an event to a Redis pub/sub channel.\n\n    Args:\n        redis_client: Async Redis client\n        channel: Target pub/sub channel (use PubSubChannel enum)\n        event: Event payload (Pydantic model or dict)\n\n    Returns:\n        Number of subscribers that received the message\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize channel to string\n    channel_str = channel.value if isinstance(channel, PubSubChannel) else channel\n\n    # Serialize event\n    if isinstance(event, BaseModel):\n        payload = event.model_dump_json()\n    else:\n        payload = json.dumps(event, default=str)\n\n    # Publish\n    subscriber_count = await redis_client.publish(channel_str, payload)\n\n    logger.debug(\n        \"pubsub.event_published\",\n        channel=channel_str,\n        event_type=event.event if isinstance(event, BaseEvent) else event.get(\"event\"),\n        subscribers=subscriber_count,\n    )\n\n    return subscriber_count\n\n\n# ─── Convenience Publishers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nasync def publish_application_status(\n    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n    pipeline_id: UUID,\n    candidate_id: UUID,\n    status: str,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Publish an application pipeline status update.\"\"\"\n    event = AgentStatusEvent(\n        pipeline_id=str(pipeline_id),\n        candidate_id=str(candidate_id),\n        status=status,\n    )\n    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.APPLICATION, event)\n\n\nasync def publish_subagent_status(\n    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n    execution_id: UUID,\n    agent_name: str,\n    pipeline_id: UUID,\n    status: str,\n    attempt: int = 1,\n    duration_ms: Optional[int] = None,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Publish a sub-agent execution status update.\"\"\"\n    event = SubAgentStatusEvent(\n        execution_id=str(execution_id),\n        agent_name=agent_name,\n        pipeline_id=str(pipeline_id),\n        status=status,\n        attempt=attempt,\n        duration_ms=duration_ms,\n    )\n    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.SUBAGENT, event)\n\n\nasync def publish_digest_ready(\n    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n    digest_id: UUID,\n    candidate_id: UUID,\n    run_date: str,\n    total_discovered: int,\n    total_scored: int,\n    top_picks_count: int,\n    hot_picks_count: int,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Publish a digest completion event.\"\"\"\n    event = DigestReadyEvent(\n        digest_id=str(digest_id),\n        candidate_id=str(candidate_id),\n        run_date=run_date,\n        total_discovered=total_discovered,\n        total_scored=total_scored,\n        top_picks_count=top_picks_count,\n        hot_picks_count=hot_picks_count,\n    )\n    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.DISCOVERY, event)\n\n\nasync def publish_crawl_status(\n    redis_client: aioredis.Redis,\n    crawl_run_id: UUID,\n    candidate_id: UUID,\n    status: str,\n    jobs_discovered: Optional[int] = None,\n    jobs_scored: Optional[int] = None,\n    error: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Publish a crawl run status update.\"\"\"\n    event = CrawlStatusEvent(\n        crawl_run_id=str(crawl_run_id),\n        candidate_id=str(candidate_id),\n        status=status,\n        jobs_discovered=jobs_discovered,\n        jobs_scored=jobs_scored,\n        error=error,\n    )\n    return await publish_event(redis_client, PubSubChannel.DISCOVERY, event)\n","numLines":322,"startLine":1,"totalLines":322}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T02:51:52.459Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NLpWqpDg6N83NhGwpf7xUp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     2→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     3→\n     4→from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n     5→from typing import Optional\n     6→\n     7→import redis.asyncio as aioredis\n     8→from fastapi import FastAPI\n     9→from fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n    10→\n    11→from backend.config import settings\n    12→from backend.observability import configure_logging, get_logger, HealthResponse\n    13→from backend.observability.health import build_health_response\n    14→from backend.database import engine, Base, AsyncSessionLocal\n    15→from backend.api.router import router\n    16→from backend.api import events as events_router\n    17→from backend.seed import seed_admin_user\n    18→\n    19→logger = get_logger(__name__)\n    20→\n    21→# Global Redis client — initialized at startup\n    22→_redis_client: Optional[aioredis.Redis] = None\n    23→\n    24→\n    25→async def get_redis() -> aioredis.Redis:\n    26→    \"\"\"FastAPI dependency that returns the global Redis client.\"\"\"\n    27→    global _redis_client\n    28→    if _redis_client is None:\n    29→        _redis_client = aioredis.from_url(\n    30→            settings.redis_url,\n    31→            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    32→            decode_responses=True,\n    33→        )\n    34→    return _redis_client\n    35→\n    36→\n    37→@asynccontextmanager\n    38→async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    39→    \"\"\"Manage application startup and shutdown lifecycle.\"\"\"\n    40→    global _redis_client\n    41→\n    42→    # Configure structured logging with PII redaction\n    43→    configure_logging()\n    44→    logger.info(\"talent-agent starting\", env=settings.app_env, version=settings.app_version)\n    45→\n    46→    # Initialize database tables\n    47→    async with engine.begin() as conn:\n    48→        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n    49→\n    50→    # Initialize Redis connection\n    51→    _redis_client = aioredis.from_url(\n    52→        settings.redis_url,\n    53→        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    54→        decode_responses=True,\n    55→    )\n    56→\n    57→    # Auto-seed admin user (Space Cowboy #9) if no users exist\n    58→    await seed_admin_user()\n    59→\n    60→    yield\n    61→\n    62→    # Cleanup\n    63→    logger.info(\"talent-agent shutting down\")\n    64→    if _redis_client:\n    65→        await _redis_client.close()\n    66→    await engine.dispose()\n    67→\n    68→\n    69→# OpenAPI docs only in non-prod environments\n    70→# Contract: HYPHA-API.md Acceptance Criteria\n    71→_docs_url = \"/docs\" if settings.debug else None\n    72→_openapi_url = \"/openapi.json\" if settings.debug else None\n    73→\n    74→app = FastAPI(\n    75→    title=\"Talent Agent API\",\n    76→    version=settings.app_version,\n    77→    lifespan=lifespan,\n    78→    docs_url=_docs_url,\n    79→    openapi_url=_openapi_url,\n    80→    redoc_url=None,  # Use Swagger UI only\n    81→)\n    82→\n    83→# CORS origins: explicit localhost for dev, production domain for prod\n    84→# Contract: HYPHA-API.md Acceptance Criteria\n    85→_cors_origins = (\n    86→    [\"http://localhost:5173\", \"http://127.0.0.1:5173\"]\n    87→    if settings.debug\n    88→    else [\"https://seanyoung.biz\"]\n    89→)\n    90→\n    91→app.add_middleware(\n    92→    CORSMiddleware,\n    93→    allow_origins=_cors_origins,\n    94→    allow_credentials=True,\n    95→    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    96→    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n    97→)\n    98→\n    99→app.include_router(router)\n   100→\n   101→# SSE event stream at /events/stream (no prefix)\n   102→# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS → GET /events/stream\n   103→app.include_router(events_router.router, prefix=\"/events\", tags=[\"events\"])\n   104→\n   105→\n   106→@app.get(\"/health\", response_model=HealthResponse)\n   107→async def health():\n   108→    \"\"\"\n   109→    Health check endpoint.\n   110→\n   111→    Returns service status, version, git SHA, and dependency health.\n   112→    Contract: NUTRIENTS.md API_CONTRACTS → GET /health\n   113→    \"\"\"\n   114→    global _redis_client\n   115→\n   116→    # Get a fresh DB session for health check\n   117→    async with AsyncSessionLocal() as db:\n   118→        return await build_health_response(\n   119→            redis_client=_redis_client,\n   120→            db_session=db,\n   121→        )\n   122→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4abf431d-40e8-4b65-91bf-402517737050","uuid":"25156bee-37c3-4228-9ea2-cc9b73256db6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/backend/main.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nimport redis.asyncio as aioredis\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n\nfrom backend.config import settings\nfrom backend.observability import configure_logging, get_logger, HealthResponse\nfrom backend.observability.health import build_health_response\nfrom backend.database import engine, Base, AsyncSessionLocal\nfrom backend.api.router import router\nfrom backend.api import events as events_router\nfrom backend.seed import seed_admin_user\n\nlogger = get_logger(__name__)\n\n# Global Redis client — initialized at startup\n_redis_client: Optional[aioredis.Redis] = None\n\n\nasync def get_redis() -> aioredis.Redis:\n    \"\"\"FastAPI dependency that returns the global Redis client.\"\"\"\n    global _redis_client\n    if _redis_client is None:\n        _redis_client = aioredis.from_url(\n            settings.redis_url,\n            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n            decode_responses=True,\n        )\n    return _redis_client\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    \"\"\"Manage application startup and shutdown lifecycle.\"\"\"\n    global _redis_client\n\n    # Configure structured logging with PII redaction\n    configure_logging()\n    logger.info(\"talent-agent starting\", env=settings.app_env, version=settings.app_version)\n\n    # Initialize database tables\n    async with engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    # Initialize Redis connection\n    _redis_client = aioredis.from_url(\n        settings.redis_url,\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n        decode_responses=True,\n    )\n\n    # Auto-seed admin user (Space Cowboy #9) if no users exist\n    await seed_admin_user()\n\n    yield\n\n    # Cleanup\n    logger.info(\"talent-agent shutting down\")\n    if _redis_client:\n        await _redis_client.close()\n    await engine.dispose()\n\n\n# OpenAPI docs only in non-prod environments\n# Contract: HYPHA-API.md Acceptance Criteria\n_docs_url = \"/docs\" if settings.debug else None\n_openapi_url = \"/openapi.json\" if settings.debug else None\n\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"Talent Agent API\",\n    version=settings.app_version,\n    lifespan=lifespan,\n    docs_url=_docs_url,\n    openapi_url=_openapi_url,\n    redoc_url=None,  # Use Swagger UI only\n)\n\n# CORS origins: explicit localhost for dev, production domain for prod\n# Contract: HYPHA-API.md Acceptance Criteria\n_cors_origins = (\n    [\"http://localhost:5173\", \"http://127.0.0.1:5173\"]\n    if settings.debug\n    else [\"https://seanyoung.biz\"]\n)\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=_cors_origins,\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\napp.include_router(router)\n\n# SSE event stream at /events/stream (no prefix)\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS → GET /events/stream\napp.include_router(events_router.router, prefix=\"/events\", tags=[\"events\"])\n\n\n@app.get(\"/health\", response_model=HealthResponse)\nasync def health():\n    \"\"\"\n    Health check endpoint.\n\n    Returns service status, version, git SHA, and dependency health.\n    Contract: NUTRIENTS.md API_CONTRACTS → GET /health\n    \"\"\"\n    global _redis_client\n\n    # Get a fresh DB session for health check\n    async with AsyncSessionLocal() as db:\n        return await build_health_response(\n            redis_client=_redis_client,\n            db_session=db,\n        )\n","numLines":122,"startLine":1,"totalLines":122}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T02:51:52.467Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ak7wJaoU1inZvX3RnQZYJU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     2→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     3→\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→Authentication API — passwordless magic link flow.\n     6→\n     7→POST  /auth/request-link     → request a magic login link\n     8→POST  /auth/verify            → verify magic link token, return JWT\n     9→GET   /auth/me                → get current authenticated user\n    10→\"\"\"\n    11→\n    12→import uuid\n    13→import secrets\n    14→from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n    15→\n    16→import jwt\n    17→import resend\n    18→import structlog\n    19→from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException, Request\n    20→from fastapi.security import HTTPBearer, HTTPAuthorizationCredentials\n    21→from pydantic import BaseModel, EmailStr\n    22→from sqlalchemy import select\n    23→from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\n    24→\n    25→from backend.config import settings\n    26→from backend.database import get_db\n    27→from backend.models.auth import User, MagicLink\n    28→\n    29→logger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\n    30→router = APIRouter()\n    31→security = HTTPBearer(auto_error=False)\n    32→\n    33→\n    34→# ─── PII Redaction ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    35→\n    36→def redact_email(email: str) -> str:\n    37→    \"\"\"Redact email for safe logging. e.g. 'spy@seanyoung.biz' → 's**@s***.biz'\"\"\"\n    38→    if not email or \"@\" not in email:\n    39→        return \"[redacted]\"\n    40→    local, domain = email.split(\"@\", 1)\n    41→    domain_parts = domain.rsplit(\".\", 1)\n    42→    redacted_local = local[0] + \"**\" if local else \"**\"\n    43→    if len(domain_parts) == 2:\n    44→        redacted_domain = domain_parts[0][0] + \"***.\" + domain_parts[1]\n    45→    else:\n    46→        redacted_domain = \"***\"\n    47→    return f\"{redacted_local}@{redacted_domain}\"\n    48→\n    49→\n    50→# ─── Schemas ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    51→\n    52→class RequestLinkPayload(BaseModel):\n    53→    \"\"\"Payload to request a magic link.\"\"\"\n    54→    email: EmailStr\n    55→\n    56→\n    57→class RequestLinkResponse(BaseModel):\n    58→    \"\"\"Response after requesting a magic link.\"\"\"\n    59→    message: str\n    60→    # In dev mode, we return the magic link directly so you can click it\n    61→    magic_link: str | None = None\n    62→    token: str | None = None\n    63→\n    64→\n    65→class VerifyTokenPayload(BaseModel):\n    66→    \"\"\"Payload to verify a magic link token.\"\"\"\n    67→    token: str\n    68→\n    69→\n    70→class AuthResponse(BaseModel):\n    71→    \"\"\"Response with JWT access token.\"\"\"\n    72→    access_token: str\n    73→    token_type: str = \"bearer\"\n    74→    user_id: str\n    75→    email: str\n    76→    is_onboarded: bool\n    77→\n    78→\n    79→class UserResponse(BaseModel):\n    80→    \"\"\"Current user info.\"\"\"\n    81→    id: str\n    82→    email: str\n    83→    name: str | None\n    84→    is_onboarded: bool\n    85→    candidate_id: str | None\n    86→    created_at: str\n    87→\n    88→\n    89→# ─── JWT Helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    90→\n    91→def create_jwt(user_id: uuid.UUID, email: str) -> str:\n    92→    \"\"\"Create a JWT access token for an authenticated user.\"\"\"\n    93→    payload = {\n    94→        \"sub\": str(user_id),\n    95→        \"email\": email,\n    96→        \"iat\": datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n    97→        \"exp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=7),\n    98→    }\n    99→    return jwt.encode(payload, settings.jwt_secret, algorithm=\"HS256\")\n   100→\n   101→\n   102→def decode_jwt(token: str) -> dict:\n   103→    \"\"\"Decode and validate a JWT token.\"\"\"\n   104→    try:\n   105→        return jwt.decode(token, settings.jwt_secret, algorithms=[\"HS256\"])\n   106→    except jwt.ExpiredSignatureError:\n   107→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Token expired\")\n   108→    except jwt.InvalidTokenError:\n   109→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid token\")\n   110→\n   111→\n   112→# ─── Resend Email ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   113→\n   114→async def send_magic_link_email(email: str, magic_link_url: str) -> bool:\n   115→    \"\"\"\n   116→    Send magic link email via Resend.\n   117→\n   118→    Returns True if email was sent successfully, False otherwise.\n   119→    Falls back gracefully if Resend is not configured.\n   120→    \"\"\"\n   121→    if not settings.resend_api_key:\n   122→        logger.warning(\n   123→            \"auth.resend_not_configured\",\n   124→            email_redacted=redact_email(email),\n   125→            message=\"Resend API key not set, email not sent\",\n   126→        )\n   127→        return False\n   128→\n   129→    resend.api_key = settings.resend_api_key\n   130→\n   131→    try:\n   132→        resend.Emails.send({\n   133→            \"from\": settings.resend_from_email,\n   134→            \"to\": email,\n   135→            \"subject\": \"Your Talent Agent Login Link\",\n   136→            \"html\": f\"\"\"\n   137→            <div style=\"font-family: 'DM Sans', -apple-system, sans-serif; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px; background-color: #0A0A0A; color: #FAFAFA;\">\n   138→                <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; color: #C9A227; font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n   139→                    Talent Agent\n   140→                </h1>\n   141→                <p style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n   142→                    Click the button below to sign in to your account. This link expires in {settings.magic_link_expiry_minutes} minutes.\n   143→                </p>\n   144→                <a href=\"{magic_link_url}\" style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #C9A227; color: #0A0A0A; padding: 14px 28px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px;\">\n   145→                    Sign In\n   146→                </a>\n   147→                <p style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #737373; margin-top: 32px; line-height: 1.6;\">\n   148→                    If you didn't request this link, you can safely ignore this email.\n   149→                </p>\n   150→                <hr style=\"border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin: 32px 0;\">\n   151→                <p style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #737373;\">\n   152→                    VibeSpace LLC · The Dot Connects\n   153→                </p>\n   154→            </div>\n   155→            \"\"\",\n   156→        })\n   157→        logger.info(\n   158→            \"auth.email_sent\",\n   159→            email_redacted=redact_email(email),\n   160→        )\n   161→        return True\n   162→    except Exception as e:\n   163→        logger.error(\n   164→            \"auth.email_send_failed\",\n   165→            email_redacted=redact_email(email),\n   166→            error=str(e),\n   167→        )\n   168→        return False\n   169→\n   170→\n   171→# ─── Auth Dependency ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   172→\n   173→async def get_current_user(\n   174→    credentials: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials | None = Depends(security),\n   175→    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n   176→) -> User:\n   177→    \"\"\"FastAPI dependency that returns the current authenticated user.\"\"\"\n   178→    if credentials is None:\n   179→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Not authenticated\")\n   180→\n   181→    payload = decode_jwt(credentials.credentials)\n   182→    user_id = payload.get(\"sub\")\n   183→    if not user_id:\n   184→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid token payload\")\n   185→\n   186→    result = await db.execute(\n   187→        select(User).where(User.id == uuid.UUID(user_id))\n   188→    )\n   189→    user = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n   190→    if not user or not user.is_active:\n   191→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"User not found or inactive\")\n   192→\n   193→    return user\n   194→\n   195→\n   196→# ─── Endpoints ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   197→\n   198→@router.post(\"/request-link\", response_model=RequestLinkResponse)\n   199→async def request_magic_link(\n   200→    payload: RequestLinkPayload,\n   201→    request: Request,\n   202→    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n   203→):\n   204→    \"\"\"\n   205→    Request a magic login link. Creates user if they don't exist.\n   206→\n   207→    In dev mode (DEBUG=true), returns the magic link directly in the response\n   208→    so you can click it without needing email infrastructure.\n   209→    In production, sends the link via Resend email service.\n   210→    \"\"\"\n   211→    email = payload.email.lower().strip()\n   212→    email_redacted = redact_email(email)\n   213→\n   214→    # Find or create user\n   215→    result = await db.execute(select(User).where(User.email == email))\n   216→    user = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n   217→\n   218→    if not user:\n   219→        user = User(email=email)\n   220→        db.add(user)\n   221→        await db.flush()\n   222→        logger.info(\n   223→            \"auth.user_created\",\n   224→            email_redacted=email_redacted,\n   225→            user_id=str(user.id),\n   226→        )\n   227→\n   228→    # Generate magic link token\n   229→    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(48)\n   230→    expires_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(minutes=settings.magic_link_expiry_minutes)\n   231→\n   232→    magic_link_record = MagicLink(\n   233→        user_id=user.id,\n   234→        token=token,\n   235→        expires_at=expires_at,\n   236→    )\n   237→    db.add(magic_link_record)\n   238→    await db.commit()\n   239→\n   240→    # Build the magic link URL using frontend origin\n   241→    origin = request.headers.get(\"origin\", \"http://localhost:5173\")\n   242→    magic_link_url = f\"{origin}/auth/verify?token={token}\"\n   243→\n   244→    logger.info(\n   245→        \"auth.magic_link_created\",\n   246→        email_redacted=email_redacted,\n   247→        expires_at=expires_at.isoformat(),\n   248→    )\n   249→\n   250→    if settings.debug:\n   251→        # Dev mode: return link directly for easy testing\n   252→        return RequestLinkResponse(\n   253→            message=\"Magic link created. Click to log in.\",\n   254→            magic_link=magic_link_url,\n   255→            token=token,\n   256→        )\n   257→    else:\n   258→        # Production: send email via Resend\n   259→        email_sent = await send_magic_link_email(email, magic_link_url)\n   260→        if email_sent:\n   261→            return RequestLinkResponse(\n   262→                message=\"Check your email for a login link.\",\n   263→            )\n   264→        else:\n   265→            # Graceful degradation if email fails\n   266→            logger.warning(\n   267→                \"auth.email_fallback\",\n   268→                email_redacted=email_redacted,\n   269→                message=\"Email service unavailable\",\n   270→            )\n   271→            return RequestLinkResponse(\n   272→                message=\"Check your email for a login link.\",\n   273→            )\n   274→\n   275→\n   276→@router.post(\"/verify\", response_model=AuthResponse)\n   277→async def verify_magic_link(\n   278→    payload: VerifyTokenPayload,\n   279→    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n   280→):\n   281→    \"\"\"\n   282→    Verify a magic link token and return a JWT access token.\n   283→\n   284→    The magic link token is single-use and time-limited.\n   285→    \"\"\"\n   286→    result = await db.execute(\n   287→        select(MagicLink).where(MagicLink.token == payload.token)\n   288→    )\n   289→    magic_link = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n   290→\n   291→    if not magic_link:\n   292→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid or expired link\")\n   293→\n   294→    if magic_link.is_used:\n   295→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"This link has already been used\")\n   296→\n   297→    if magic_link.expires_at.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) < datetime.now(timezone.utc):\n   298→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"This link has expired\")\n   299→\n   300→    # Mark as used\n   301→    magic_link.is_used = True\n   302→\n   303→    # Get the user\n   304→    user_result = await db.execute(\n   305→        select(User).where(User.id == magic_link.user_id)\n   306→    )\n   307→    user = user_result.scalar_one_or_none()\n   308→    if not user:\n   309→        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"User not found\")\n   310→\n   311→    # Update last login\n   312→    user.last_login_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n   313→    await db.commit()\n   314→\n   315→    # Issue JWT\n   316→    access_token = create_jwt(user.id, user.email)\n   317→\n   318→    logger.info(\n   319→        \"auth.login_success\",\n   320→        email_redacted=redact_email(user.email),\n   321→        user_id=str(user.id),\n   322→    )\n   323→\n   324→    return AuthResponse(\n   325→        access_token=access_token,\n   326→        user_id=str(user.id),\n   327→        email=user.email,\n   328→        is_onboarded=user.is_onboarded,\n   329→    )\n   330→\n   331→\n   332→@router.get(\"/me\", response_model=UserResponse)\n   333→async def get_me(\n   334→    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user),\n   335→):\n   336→    \"\"\"Get the current authenticated user's info.\"\"\"\n   337→    return UserResponse(\n   338→        id=str(current_user.id),\n   339→        email=current_user.email,\n   340→        name=current_user.name,\n   341→        is_onboarded=current_user.is_onboarded,\n   342→        candidate_id=str(current_user.candidate_id) if current_user.candidate_id else None,\n   343→        created_at=current_user.created_at.isoformat(),\n   344→    )\n   345→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4abf431d-40e8-4b65-91bf-402517737050","uuid":"ec9e7fc7-ad46-4ca5-9e30-d57f672a36cc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/backend/api/auth.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n\"\"\"\nAuthentication API — passwordless magic link flow.\n\nPOST  /auth/request-link     → request a magic login link\nPOST  /auth/verify            → verify magic link token, return JWT\nGET   /auth/me                → get current authenticated user\n\"\"\"\n\nimport uuid\nimport secrets\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\nimport jwt\nimport resend\nimport structlog\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException, Request\nfrom fastapi.security import HTTPBearer, HTTPAuthorizationCredentials\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, EmailStr\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\n\nfrom backend.config import settings\nfrom backend.database import get_db\nfrom backend.models.auth import User, MagicLink\n\nlogger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\nrouter = APIRouter()\nsecurity = HTTPBearer(auto_error=False)\n\n\n# ─── PII Redaction ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef redact_email(email: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Redact email for safe logging. e.g. 'spy@seanyoung.biz' → 's**@s***.biz'\"\"\"\n    if not email or \"@\" not in email:\n        return \"[redacted]\"\n    local, domain = email.split(\"@\", 1)\n    domain_parts = domain.rsplit(\".\", 1)\n    redacted_local = local[0] + \"**\" if local else \"**\"\n    if len(domain_parts) == 2:\n        redacted_domain = domain_parts[0][0] + \"***.\" + domain_parts[1]\n    else:\n        redacted_domain = \"***\"\n    return f\"{redacted_local}@{redacted_domain}\"\n\n\n# ─── Schemas ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nclass RequestLinkPayload(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Payload to request a magic link.\"\"\"\n    email: EmailStr\n\n\nclass RequestLinkResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response after requesting a magic link.\"\"\"\n    message: str\n    # In dev mode, we return the magic link directly so you can click it\n    magic_link: str | None = None\n    token: str | None = None\n\n\nclass VerifyTokenPayload(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Payload to verify a magic link token.\"\"\"\n    token: str\n\n\nclass AuthResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response with JWT access token.\"\"\"\n    access_token: str\n    token_type: str = \"bearer\"\n    user_id: str\n    email: str\n    is_onboarded: bool\n\n\nclass UserResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Current user info.\"\"\"\n    id: str\n    email: str\n    name: str | None\n    is_onboarded: bool\n    candidate_id: str | None\n    created_at: str\n\n\n# ─── JWT Helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef create_jwt(user_id: uuid.UUID, email: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Create a JWT access token for an authenticated user.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"sub\": str(user_id),\n        \"email\": email,\n        \"iat\": datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        \"exp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=7),\n    }\n    return jwt.encode(payload, settings.jwt_secret, algorithm=\"HS256\")\n\n\ndef decode_jwt(token: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Decode and validate a JWT token.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return jwt.decode(token, settings.jwt_secret, algorithms=[\"HS256\"])\n    except jwt.ExpiredSignatureError:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Token expired\")\n    except jwt.InvalidTokenError:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid token\")\n\n\n# ─── Resend Email ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync def send_magic_link_email(email: str, magic_link_url: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Send magic link email via Resend.\n\n    Returns True if email was sent successfully, False otherwise.\n    Falls back gracefully if Resend is not configured.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not settings.resend_api_key:\n        logger.warning(\n            \"auth.resend_not_configured\",\n            email_redacted=redact_email(email),\n            message=\"Resend API key not set, email not sent\",\n        )\n        return False\n\n    resend.api_key = settings.resend_api_key\n\n    try:\n        resend.Emails.send({\n            \"from\": settings.resend_from_email,\n            \"to\": email,\n            \"subject\": \"Your Talent Agent Login Link\",\n            \"html\": f\"\"\"\n            <div style=\"font-family: 'DM Sans', -apple-system, sans-serif; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px; background-color: #0A0A0A; color: #FAFAFA;\">\n                <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; color: #C9A227; font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n                    Talent Agent\n                </h1>\n                <p style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n                    Click the button below to sign in to your account. This link expires in {settings.magic_link_expiry_minutes} minutes.\n                </p>\n                <a href=\"{magic_link_url}\" style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #C9A227; color: #0A0A0A; padding: 14px 28px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px;\">\n                    Sign In\n                </a>\n                <p style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #737373; margin-top: 32px; line-height: 1.6;\">\n                    If you didn't request this link, you can safely ignore this email.\n                </p>\n                <hr style=\"border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin: 32px 0;\">\n                <p style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #737373;\">\n                    VibeSpace LLC · The Dot Connects\n                </p>\n            </div>\n            \"\"\",\n        })\n        logger.info(\n            \"auth.email_sent\",\n            email_redacted=redact_email(email),\n        )\n        return True\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(\n            \"auth.email_send_failed\",\n            email_redacted=redact_email(email),\n            error=str(e),\n        )\n        return False\n\n\n# ─── Auth Dependency ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync def get_current_user(\n    credentials: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials | None = Depends(security),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n) -> User:\n    \"\"\"FastAPI dependency that returns the current authenticated user.\"\"\"\n    if credentials is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Not authenticated\")\n\n    payload = decode_jwt(credentials.credentials)\n    user_id = payload.get(\"sub\")\n    if not user_id:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid token payload\")\n\n    result = await db.execute(\n        select(User).where(User.id == uuid.UUID(user_id))\n    )\n    user = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n    if not user or not user.is_active:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"User not found or inactive\")\n\n    return user\n\n\n# ─── Endpoints ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n@router.post(\"/request-link\", response_model=RequestLinkResponse)\nasync def request_magic_link(\n    payload: RequestLinkPayload,\n    request: Request,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Request a magic login link. Creates user if they don't exist.\n\n    In dev mode (DEBUG=true), returns the magic link directly in the response\n    so you can click it without needing email infrastructure.\n    In production, sends the link via Resend email service.\n    \"\"\"\n    email = payload.email.lower().strip()\n    email_redacted = redact_email(email)\n\n    # Find or create user\n    result = await db.execute(select(User).where(User.email == email))\n    user = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n\n    if not user:\n        user = User(email=email)\n        db.add(user)\n        await db.flush()\n        logger.info(\n            \"auth.user_created\",\n            email_redacted=email_redacted,\n            user_id=str(user.id),\n        )\n\n    # Generate magic link token\n    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(48)\n    expires_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(minutes=settings.magic_link_expiry_minutes)\n\n    magic_link_record = MagicLink(\n        user_id=user.id,\n        token=token,\n        expires_at=expires_at,\n    )\n    db.add(magic_link_record)\n    await db.commit()\n\n    # Build the magic link URL using frontend origin\n    origin = request.headers.get(\"origin\", \"http://localhost:5173\")\n    magic_link_url = f\"{origin}/auth/verify?token={token}\"\n\n    logger.info(\n        \"auth.magic_link_created\",\n        email_redacted=email_redacted,\n        expires_at=expires_at.isoformat(),\n    )\n\n    if settings.debug:\n        # Dev mode: return link directly for easy testing\n        return RequestLinkResponse(\n            message=\"Magic link created. Click to log in.\",\n            magic_link=magic_link_url,\n            token=token,\n        )\n    else:\n        # Production: send email via Resend\n        email_sent = await send_magic_link_email(email, magic_link_url)\n        if email_sent:\n            return RequestLinkResponse(\n                message=\"Check your email for a login link.\",\n            )\n        else:\n            # Graceful degradation if email fails\n            logger.warning(\n                \"auth.email_fallback\",\n                email_redacted=email_redacted,\n                message=\"Email service unavailable\",\n            )\n            return RequestLinkResponse(\n                message=\"Check your email for a login link.\",\n            )\n\n\n@router.post(\"/verify\", response_model=AuthResponse)\nasync def verify_magic_link(\n    payload: VerifyTokenPayload,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Verify a magic link token and return a JWT access token.\n\n    The magic link token is single-use and time-limited.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = await db.execute(\n        select(MagicLink).where(MagicLink.token == payload.token)\n    )\n    magic_link = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n\n    if not magic_link:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"Invalid or expired link\")\n\n    if magic_link.is_used:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"This link has already been used\")\n\n    if magic_link.expires_at.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) < datetime.now(timezone.utc):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"This link has expired\")\n\n    # Mark as used\n    magic_link.is_used = True\n\n    # Get the user\n    user_result = await db.execute(\n        select(User).where(User.id == magic_link.user_id)\n    )\n    user = user_result.scalar_one_or_none()\n    if not user:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"User not found\")\n\n    # Update last login\n    user.last_login_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n    await db.commit()\n\n    # Issue JWT\n    access_token = create_jwt(user.id, user.email)\n\n    logger.info(\n        \"auth.login_success\",\n        email_redacted=redact_email(user.email),\n        user_id=str(user.id),\n    )\n\n    return AuthResponse(\n        access_token=access_token,\n        user_id=str(user.id),\n        email=user.email,\n        is_onboarded=user.is_onboarded,\n    )\n\n\n@router.get(\"/me\", response_model=UserResponse)\nasync def get_me(\n    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user),\n):\n    \"\"\"Get the current authenticated user's info.\"\"\"\n    return UserResponse(\n        id=str(current_user.id),\n        email=current_user.email,\n        name=current_user.name,\n        is_onboarded=current_user.is_onboarded,\n        candidate_id=str(current_user.candidate_id) if current_user.candidate_id else None,\n        created_at=current_user.created_at.isoformat(),\n    )\n","numLines":345,"startLine":1,"totalLines":345}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T02:52:00.862Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01FFkyAucEHhmR8Jd6FDjCRA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have a complete picture of the codebase. Looking at the current `backend/api/events.py`, I see it already has the core structure but the SSE generator has an issue. According to my scope (api-streaming-agent.subscriber):\n\n**Scope:** `backend/api/events.py — Redis pub/sub subscriber with channel allowlist`\n\nThe file exists, but I need to review it against the acceptance criteria from HYPHA-API-STREAMING.md. Looking at the code, there's an issue with the Redis message handling: the `message[\"data\"]` could be bytes when `decode_responses=False`, but `get_redis()` in `main.py` uses `decode_responses=True`, so it should be string.\n\nHowever, I notice the generator yields the message data directly without ensuring it's a string (if bytes come through, it could break). Let me verify the existing implementation is correct and check if there are any issues:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12928,"cache_read_input_tokens":54281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12928,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4abf431d-40e8-4b65-91bf-402517737050","uuid":"48af8c93-e157-4f94-87f5-c94e8b30d3fb"}}
