{"t":"2026-05-28T02:52:45.644Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_016UT24VC7W6c5UJZMvSBD4i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The virtualenv was created on a different machine. Let me analyze the code manually. Looking at `backend/api/events.py`, the implementation appears comprehensive but I want to verify it meets all the acceptance criteria from HYPHA-API-STREAMING.md:\n\n**Acceptance Criteria Status Check:**\n1. ✅ `GET /events/stream?channel=agent.status.discovery` returns `Content-Type: text/event-stream`\n2. ✅ Request requires valid JWT via `Authorization: Bearer` header (via `get_current_user`)\n3. ✅ 401 returned if JWT is missing, invalid, or expired\n4. ✅ 400 returned if `channel` is not in allowlist\n5. ✅ Each published Redis message appears as SSE frame: `data: {json}\\n\\n`\n6. ✅ Heartbeat `:ping\\n\\n` emitted every 15 seconds\n7. ✅ Backpressure: if client queue exceeds 100 messages, drop oldest and emit `event: slow_client\\ndata: {\"dropped\": N}\\n\\n`\n8. ✅ Proper connection cleanup when client disconnects\n\nLooking at my specific scope (`api-streaming-agent.subscriber`), the subscriber logic (the `reader_task` function inside `sse_event_generator`) is already implemented. Let me check if there are any improvements needed for the subscriber portion specifically.\n\nLooking at the code more carefully, I notice the data handling in the reader_task. Since `get_redis()` uses `decode_responses=True`, the message data will be a string. However, the current code doesn't explicitly handle the case where `message[\"data\"]` might need string conversion for safety.\n\nLet me also check if the message decoding is correct. The Redis message data when using `decode_responses=True` will be a string, so the current implementation should work. However, I see that the slow_client event format uses a raw f-string with curly braces that could be an issue:\n\n```python\nyield f\"event: slow_client\\ndata: {{\\\"dropped\\\": {dropped_count}}}\\n\\n\"\n```\n\nThis looks correct because `{{` and `}}` escape to literal `{` and `}` in f-strings.\n\nThe code looks complete and correct. Let me verify the file doesn't have any syntax issues by checking imports and structure:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152,"cache_read_input_tokens":68368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":152,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4abf431d-40e8-4b65-91bf-402517737050","uuid":"1f419c55-8569-4bdc-ae14-040c57bb6447"}}
