{"t":"2026-05-28T02:52:59.695Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01HzanZNmx6mRs2Meimi79cb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file has valid syntax. Now let me double-check that the subscriber implementation covers all the requirements from my scope. Looking at the mycelium.yaml again for my specific leaf:\n\n```yaml\n- id: api-streaming-agent.subscriber\n  scope: backend/api/events.py — Redis pub/sub subscriber with channel allowlist\n```\n\nThe subscriber component needs to:\n1. ✅ Subscribe to Redis pub/sub channels\n2. ✅ Have a channel allowlist (`ALLOWED_CHANNELS` frozenset)\n3. ✅ Read messages from the subscription\n4. ✅ Handle the subscription lifecycle (subscribe, unsubscribe, cleanup)\n\nThe current implementation in `backend/api/events.py` has all of this. The `reader_task` function inside `sse_event_generator` handles:\n- Subscribing to the channel via `await pubsub.subscribe(channel)`\n- Listening for messages via `async for message in pubsub.listen()`\n- Properly filtering message types (`if message[\"type\"] == \"message\"`)\n- Cleanup in the `finally` block (unsubscribe + close)\n\nThe channel allowlist is properly defined:\n```python\nALLOWED_CHANNELS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\n    PubSubChannel.DISCOVERY.value,    # agent.status.discovery\n    PubSubChannel.APPLICATION.value,  # agent.status.application\n})\n```\n\nAnd validated in the endpoint:\n```python\nif channel not in ALLOWED_CHANNELS:\n    allowed_list = \", \".join(sorted(ALLOWED_CHANNELS))\n    raise HTTPException(\n        status_code=400,\n        detail=f\"Invalid channel. Allowed: {allowed_list}\",\n    )\n```\n\nThe implementation is complete and meets all acceptance criteria. The file is already in place and correctly implemented. My role as the `api-streaming-agent.subscriber` specialist is satisfied - the Redis pub/sub subscriber with channel allowlist is fully implemented.\